ghpull:696 a bl:PullRequest, bl:WorkItem ;
    rdfs:label "owl_xml_parser: ABox axioms + remaining annotation axioms (#608)" ;
    bl:number 696 ;
    bl:state bl:Open ;
    bl:closesIssue ghissues:608 .

session:claudeSonnet5 a prov:SoftwareAgent ;
    rdfs:label "Claude Sonnet 5" .

session:pr696 a agp:AgentSession ;
    prov:wasAssociatedWith session:claudeSonnet5 ;
    prov:used ghissues:608 ;
    prov:startedAtTime "2026-10-01T14:18:52Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    prov:endedAtTime "2026-10-01T14:31:23Z"^^xsd:dateTime .

session:pr696Summary a agp:TranscriptSummary ;
    agp:summaryText "Issue #608 asked for OWL/XML parsing of the remaining ABox axioms (ClassAssertion, ObjectPropertyAssertion, NegativeObjectPropertyAssertion, DataPropertyAssertion, NegativeDataPropertyAssertion, SameIndividual, DifferentIndividuals), the remaining annotation axioms (AnnotationAssertion, SubAnnotationPropertyOf, AnnotationPropertyDomain, AnnotationPropertyRange), AnonymousIndividual fillers, and axiom-level <Annotation> children on every axiom kind -- all deferred by #605/#606/#607. crate:owl_xml_parser's provenance query returned no rows despite three existing summaries (#638/#665/#681), so read them directly instead. Consulted the advisor before coding, since AnonymousIndividual threatened a signature-cascade refactor (individual()/class_expression() both take &Prefixes). The advisor's fix -- turn iri::Prefixes from a type alias into a struct carrying next_anon/labels, mirroring owl_functional_parser's ParserContext::anon_individual_for_label -- kept every existing &Prefixes signature unchanged. Followed strict TDD (a deliberate correction from #681's one-pass precedent, per the advisor): plan-doc section first, then ~30 new/flipped #[ignore]d integration tests, then src/. New src/assertion.rs covers the seven ABox elements; annotation.rs gained split_axiom_annotations (shared helper consuming the leading axiomAnnotations run, replacing axiom.rs/property_axiom.rs's placeholder rejection), parse_iri_text_element (factored out for reuse), parse_annotation_filler_as_graph_element (mirroring owl_functional_parser's GraphElement lowering), and parse_annotation_axiom for the four remaining AnnotationAxiom elements. Verified exact OWL/XML child-element ordering against the W3C spec via WebFetch before implementing rather than guessing from the Functional-Style analogue. Filed two genuine out-of-scope follow-ups as real issues at Status Todo under epic #564 before coding: #694 (<DatatypeDefinition>) and #695 (owl_ontology::Annotation has no slot for meta-annotations, a shared type-model gap). Clippy/fmt clean. Local cargo test --workspace hit the known sparql_endpoint query_timeout SIGKILL false alarm (memory-constrained host); CI (gh pr checks --watch) came back fully green on all nine jobs." ;
    agp:reasoningFor ghpull:696 ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy session:pr696 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo session:claudeSonnet5 .

session:pr696Summary agp:decisionPoint session:pr696Decision .

session:pr696Decision a agp:Decision ;
    agp:summaryText "Turned iri::Prefixes from a plain HashMap<String,String> type alias into a struct holding the prefix map plus next_anon: Cell<u32> and labels: RefCell<HashMap<String,u32>>, giving it an anon_individual_for_label method mirroring owl_functional_parser::iri::ParserContext. This kept every existing &Prefixes function signature in the crate unchanged -- individual.rs, class_expr.rs, annotation.rs, and the new assertion.rs all just call prefixes.anon_individual_for_label(node_id) through the reference they already had." ;
    agp:alternative "Considered introducing a second parameter (e.g. an AnonIndividuals context struct threaded alongside &Prefixes) into every function that could reach an Individual or AnnotationValue position -- individual(), class_expression(), parse_annotation(), and everything that calls them transitively. Rejected on advisor consultation: this would have meant editing call sites across class_expr.rs, data_range.rs, property_expr.rs, declaration.rs, axiom.rs, property_axiom.rs, and lib.rs for a concern (anonymous-individual id assignment) that is conceptually identical to prefix resolution -- a single piece of per-document parsing state -- and the sibling parsers (owl_functional_parser, manchester_parser) already establish the precedent of folding both into one ParserContext-shaped value rather than two parallel threaded parameters." .
